/* book exam traps: The lower identifier wins, because dominant is 0 and recessive is 1. Writing "the higher priority number wins" loses the mark. | CAN FD switches only the data phase to the fast rate (BRS); arbitration and ACK stay at the nominal rate, so priority works as in classic CAN. | In CAN FD a DLC above 8 is a code, not a byte count: 9 means 12 bytes, 10 means 16 and 15 means 64. | Bus-off follows TEC above 255; error passive follows TEC or REC above 127. Do not swap the two limits. */
