/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - LIN links small body modules: window lifters, mirrors, seat motors and climate flaps.
   - The master owns a schedule table, a fixed list of frames and the time slot for each.
   - T is the nominal frame time; 34 bits is the nominal header (break and delimiter 14, sync 10, PID 10); every byte on the wire takes 10 bits (start bit, 8 data bits, stop bit); n data bytes plus 1 checksum byte make the response; τ is one bit
   - Tₘₐₓ is the longest time the frame may take; the 40 per cent margin allows for gaps between bytes.
   - FlexRay is for systems where a late message is itself a fault: active suspension, chassis control, brake-by-wire and steer-by-wire.
   - Time is divided into repeating communication cycles, typically 1 to 5 ms long and numbered 0 to 63.
   - A FlexRay frame has a 5-byte header (frame ID equal to the slot number, payload length, header CRC, cycle count), 0 to 254 payload bytes and a 24-bit CRC.
   - Office Ethernet uses two pairs (100BASE-TX) or four pairs (1000BASE-T) and heavy connectors.
   - Ethernet carries camera and radar streams, infotainment, software downloads and the backbone.
*/
