/* book exam traps: LIN is not multi-master: only the master sends headers. A slave sends only a response, and only for the frame identifiers it publishes. | The LIN header names a frame, not a slave. One frame can be read by many nodes, and the master can publish a frame itself. | FlexRay is not purely event-driven: the static segment is TDMA and gives the guarantee; only the dynamic segment is FTDMA. | Automotive Ethernet uses one pair, not the two pairs of 100BASE-TX or the four of 1000BASE-T. In a LIN frame time every byte is 10 bits, and the checksum byte counts too. */
